1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,720
Imagine Bengaluru waking up tomorrow with
absolutely no water coming from its taps.

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,690
Bengaluru depends on
multiple water sources,

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,630
including the Cauvery
River and groundwater.

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:13,830
But the city's growing population puts
enormous pressure on its water supply.

5
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:17,700
Now imagine a prolonged drought combined
with falling groundwater levels.

6
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:19,130
Apartments, offices,

7
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:22,550
restaurants and industries would
all compete for limited water.

8
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,830
Water tankers could become
even more expensive,

9
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:27,110
and some businesses might
struggle to operate.

10
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:29,300
A city can grow with
more buildings and roads.

11
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:31,340
But without water, none of it works.

12
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:34,550
Which Indian city do you think could
face the next major water crisis?

